00:08:55.397 --> 00:08:59.510
There's no excuse, or there's
nothing to justify it.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.993
But um, you know, I think
that as human beings,

00:09:01.993 --> 00:09:03.945
we all say and do things that

00:09:03.945 --> 00:09:06.345
we don't mean at all sometimes.

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:07.938
And we have to learn from it,

00:09:07.938 --> 00:09:09.322
I mean, that's part of our process.

00:09:09.322 --> 00:09:12.379
We have to learn from our
mistakes and that's how we grow.

00:09:12.379 --> 00:09:14.168
- I think a year to the day

00:09:14.168 --> 00:09:16.163
you were on The Tonight Show Jimmy Fallon,

00:09:16.163 --> 00:09:17.256
who's my, my mancrush
- Yeah.

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:18.659
I love him.
- Right, he's the best.

00:09:18.659 --> 00:09:19.992
- He's so great.
- And you got to do

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:21.920
Broadway versions of rap songs,

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.685
doing "99 Problems", "Thrift Shop",

00:09:23.685 --> 00:09:24.627
"Insane In The Membrane".

00:09:24.627 --> 00:09:25.460
- Yes.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:26.418
